diff --git a/docs/web-storefront.md b/docs/web-storefront.md
index b7aa93b..a2d858a 100644
--- a/docs/web-storefront.md
+++ b/docs/web-storefront.md
@@ -39,3 +39,6 @@ Use the dedicated `deployment/install_web_customer_addresses.py` patch for this
 Returning visitors now activate the last saved address with an automatic server discovery request; they do not resubmit or reconfirm registration. The address selector lives in the persistent site header. Selecting another saved address with an empty cart immediately rediscovers eligible stores. A nonempty cart keeps the existing clear-cart confirmation, and adding/editing an address still opens the data form. Failed automatic discovery keeps the saved summary and offers retry without asking for registration again. An uncertain prior order must be resolved before automatic discovery starts. This incremental patch requires the previous customer/address release `2c597530e88c78e39f54bc68351246732a566fa2`; it preserves its browser storage schema and saved data.
 
 The automatic-return patch additionally preserves the server session context nonce when normalized delivery fields are unchanged. Reopening the same address in another tab therefore does not invalidate an in-flight quote. Different or invalid delivery details still invalidate the former context, and every automatic discovery still rechecks current coverage. The incremental installer scopes its four files to home, storefront JS/CSS, and the existing WebStorefront service; it syntax-checks both PHP targets and performs no migration.
+
+
+The header now groups the existing store selector next to the saved destination selector. Its existing ID and event bindings are unchanged, so eligible-store filtering, selected-store state and cart-change confirmation keep their behavior. The menu heading no longer duplicates the selector. Both labels and selected values use readable colors on navy, and the controls share a compact row below the navigation on narrower screens. The layout-only incremental installer updates just home/CSS from baseline `b2ec35c91224af06bf1c8f9c2f0e54402f2291f9`.
